# Wheeltap

**17 findings** in 12 files, 670 lines.

| Severity | Count |
|---|---|
| critical | 3 |
| high | 11 |
| medium | 2 |
| low | 1 |

## Critical

### `WT001` WT001_missing_signer/vault.rs:37

`Withdraw.authority` is verified by a `has_one` constraint but is never required to sign, and no account in `Withdraw` signs at all. The constraint proves which account this is; it does not prove the holder authorised anything. Public keys are public, so any caller can pass this one.

```rust
    pub authority: AccountInfo<'info>,
```

**Fix.** Type the account as `Signer<'info>`. If it must stay an `AccountInfo`, require the signature explicitly with `#[account(signer)]` or `constraint = authority.is_signer`.

<sub>critical · confidence high · `Withdraw.authority` · id `2d70e5e62f325c65`</sub>

<sub>[reference](https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/signer-auth) · [reference](https://github.com/coral-xyz/sealevel-attacks)</sub>

### `WT002` WT002_missing_owner/oracle.rs:44

`Borrow.oracle` is an unvalidated account whose data is deserialised in `borrow` without establishing the owning program. An attacker can pass an account owned by their own program with any contents they like.

```rust
    pub oracle: AccountInfo<'info>,
```

**Fix.** Use `Account<'info, T>`, which verifies the owner and discriminator before the handler runs. If the account must stay an `AccountInfo`, pin it with `#[account(owner = expected::ID)]` or assert `*account.owner` before reading its data.

<sub>critical · confidence medium · `Borrow.oracle` · id `ffe1e9d53c4e3354`</sub>

<sub>[reference](https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/owner-checks) · [reference](https://github.com/coral-xyz/sealevel-attacks)</sub>

### `WT007` WT007_arbitrary_cpi/router.rs:55

`Forward.target_program` is invoked as a program by `forward`, but its address is never established. The caller chooses which program receives the invocation, and any signing seeds this program supplies go with it.

```rust
    pub target_program: AccountInfo<'info>,
```

**Fix.** Declare the callee as `Program<'info, T>`, or `Interface<'info, T>` where several implementations are accepted. Where no Anchor type exists, pin the address with `#[account(address = expected::ID)]`.

<sub>critical · confidence high · `Forward.target_program` · id `2f064f6836edaf41`</sub>

<sub>[reference](https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/arbitrary-cpi) · [reference](https://github.com/coral-xyz/sealevel-attacks)</sub>

## High

### `WT003` WT003_unchecked_arithmetic/staking.rs:23

`stake.amount + amount` in `deposit` uses `+` on a value that holds funds. In a release build this wraps silently rather than failing.

```rust
        stake.amount = stake.amount + amount;
```

**Fix.** Use `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` and return an error on overflow, or `saturating_*` where clamping is the intended behaviour. Alternatively set `overflow-checks = true` under `[profile.release]`, which turns wrapping into a panic and silences this rule.

<sub>high · confidence medium · `staking::deposit` · id `d2c5e1a8cb484e2e`</sub>

<sub>[reference](https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/overflow-underflow) · [reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#overflow-checks)</sub>

